        "original_id": "1d7227f7-9916-5acf-9b8e-ed3870f1c889",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William K. Howard, Clemence Dane, A. E. W. Mason, Vivien Leigh\n- Works: Fire Over England, Gone with the Wind, A Streetcar Named Desire\n- Awards: Academy Awards for Best Actress\n- Roles: Scarlett O'Hara, Blanche DuBois\n\nFacts:\n- A. E. W. Mason wrote the novel \"Fire Over England.\"\n- Clemence Dane wrote the film adaptation of \"Fire Over England,\" and William K. Howard directed it.\n- In 1939, Vivien Leigh won the Academy Award for Best Actress for playing Scarlett O'Hara in \"Gone with the Wind.\"\n- In 1949, Vivien Leigh played Blanche DuBois on stage in London's West End in \"A Streetcar Named Desire.\"\n- In 1951, Vivien Leigh won the Academy Award for Best Actress for playing Blanche DuBois in the film version of \"A Streetcar Named Desire.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
